Package: gaugeDependence
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian MCMC for Bivariate Extremes via Gauge Functions
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-06-30
Authors@R: person("Elizabeth", "Lawler", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "eslawler@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-4491-4733"))
Description: Provides adaptive Metropolis-Hastings MCMC samplers for fitting
    bivariate extreme value models within a geometric framework.
    The joint distribution of a bivariate extreme is decomposed into radial (R) 
    and angular (W) components: radii above a threshold are modelled as
    Gamma(2, g(W)), where g is a gauge function; angles are modelled via a
    star-shaped angular density. Six parametric gauge families are implemented
    (Gaussian, logistic, inverse logistic, asymmetric logistic, Dirichlet,
    rectangular), with both truncated and censored likelihood options for the
    radial component. Posterior pointwise log-likelihoods are computed for
    downstream Bayesian model averaging via the loo package. Core samplers and
    gauge functions are implemented in C++ via Rcpp and RcppArmadillo.
